# Documentation hygiene

## Canonical docs

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `docs/BRIEF.md` | The brief: concept, ethics, how the work behaves, infrastructure decisions |
| `docs/POWER.md`, `docs/MATERIALS.md`, `docs/SCANNING.md` | Light and power, print materials, scan method |
| `docs/BIBLIOGRAPHY.md` | Generated from Zotero; never edit by hand |

Add another `docs/*.md` only if it is a decision record or an ops contract the code cannot own. Default: do not add a new doc.

## Decisions: work, proposal, option

- **Work decision** (true whatever happens to any application): edit the brief body in place, then add one dated line to its Decisions log saying what changed and where. Delete log lines a later change supersedes; git keeps the history.
- **Proposal choice** (made for one call: room layout, what to include, how to pitch): never goes here. It lives with the application in the private studio repo. If the show is confirmed it becomes that show's plan there; it reaches these docs only if it holds beyond that show.
- **Option or research** (a menu, a precedent, a finding): options go in the relevant section's shortlist; precedents go to Zotero as notes on the item.

## Never commit

- Milestone or issue status diaries; ship status belongs in issues and PRs
- Phase timelines or dates in docs (dates live on issues)
- Agent routing, prompt patterns, model pickers (AGENTS.md only)
- Links to chat transcripts
- Application history, venue-specific pitch language, contact details

## Keep in sync (same PR)

| Change touches | Update |
|---|---|
| Public behavior, stack, how to run, how to fetch data not kept locally | `README.md` |
| Concept, ethics, how the work behaves, infra decisions | `docs/BRIEF.md` |
| User- or ops-visible shipping note | `CHANGELOG.md` |
